INTEGRALS OF BESSEL FUNCTIONS (p.481)
11.1.14  x^{\frac12}e^{-x}\int_0^x I_0(t)dt\sim(2\pi)^{-\frac12}\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}a_kx^{-k}
where the a_k are defined as in 11.1.12.
11.1.15  x^{\frac12}e^x\int_x^\infty K_0(t)dt\sim(\tfrac{\pi}{2})^{\frac12}\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}(-)^ka_kx^{-k}
where the a_k are defined as in 11.1.12.
Polynomial Approximations
11.1.16  8\le x\le\infty
\int_x^\infty [J_0(t)+iY_0(t)]dt=x^{-\frac12}e^{i(x-\pi/4)}\left[\sum_{k=0}^{7}(-)^ka_k(x/8)^{-2k-1}+i\sum_{k=0}^{7}(-)^kb_k(x/8)^{-2k}+\epsilon(x)\right]
|\epsilon(x)|\le2\times10^{-9}
Sample coefficients (k, a_k, b_k): 0: .06233\,47304, .79788\,45600; 7: .00002\,68482, .00002\,26238
11.1.17  8\le x\le\infty
x^{\frac12}e^{-x}\int_0^x I_0(t)dt=\sum_{k=0}^{6}d_k(x/8)^{-k}+\epsilon(x)
|\epsilon(x)|\le2\times10^{-6}
Sample coefficients (k, d_k): 0: .39894\,23; 6: -.00739\,95
11.1.18  7\le x\le\infty
x^{\frac12}e^x\int_x^\infty K_0(t)dt=\sum_{k=0}^{6}(-)^ke_k(x/7)^{-k}+\epsilon(x)
|\epsilon(x)|\le2\times10^{-7}
Sample coefficients (k, e_k): 0: 1.25331\,414; 6: .00033\,934
\int\frac{J_0(t)dt}{t},\ \int\frac{Y_0(t)dt}{t},\ \int\frac{K_0(t)dt}{t}
11.1.19  \int_0^x \frac{1-J_0(t)}{t}dt=2x^{-1}\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}(2k+3)[\psi(k+2)-\psi(1)]J_{2k+3}(x)=1-2x^{-1}J_1(x)+2x^{-1}\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}(2k+5)[\psi(k+3)-\psi(1)-1]J_{2k+5}(x)
For \psi(z), see 6.3.
11.1.20  \int_x^\infty \frac{J_0(t)dt}{t}+\gamma+\ln\tfrac{x}{2}=\int_0^x \frac{[1-J_0(t)]dt}{t}=-\sum_{k=1}^{\infty}\frac{(-)^k(x/2)^{2k}}{2k(k!)^2}
11.1.21  \int_x^\infty \frac{Y_0(t)dt}{t}=-\tfrac1\pi(\ln\tfrac{x}{2})^2-\tfrac{2\gamma}{\pi}\ln\tfrac{x}{2}+\tfrac1\pi(\tfrac{\pi^2}{6}-\gamma^2)+\tfrac2\pi\sum_{k=1}^{\infty}\frac{(-)^k(x/2)^{2k}}{2k(k!)^2}\{\psi(k+1)+\tfrac{1}{2k}-\ln\tfrac{x}{2}\}
11.1.22  \int_x^\infty \frac{K_0(t)dt}{t}=\tfrac12(\ln\tfrac{x}{2})^2+\gamma\ln\tfrac{x}{2}+\tfrac{\pi^2}{24}+\tfrac{\gamma^2}{2}-\sum_{k=1}^{\infty}\frac{(x/2)^{2k}}{2k(k!)^2}\{\psi(k+1)+\tfrac{1}{2k}-\ln\tfrac{x}{2}\}
11.1.23  \int_{-ix}^{-i\infty}... =\int_{-ix}^{\infty} \frac{K_0(t)dt}{t}=\frac{i\pi}{2}\int_x^\infty \frac{J_0(t)dt}{t}-\frac{\pi}{2}\int_x^\infty \frac{Y_0(t)dt}{t}
